            {
                "entry_id": "6a0dedea-d1c4-3839-a942-8da9042e8c87",
                "word": "Mancunian",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7a8e1b7d-91a7-42c1-9d9a-bd1179261302",
                        "entry_id": "6a0dedea-d1c4-3839-a942-8da9042e8c87",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more Mancunian"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c49f879c-5dbe-428a-962e-21fdccfe4d36",
                        "entry_id": "6a0dedea-d1c4-3839-a942-8da9042e8c87",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Mancunian"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6306228-d9ef-33bd-b4ac-396975e84816",
                        "entry_id": "6a0dedea-d1c4-3839-a942-8da9042e8c87",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Related or pertaining to Manchester, England, in the United Kingdom."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02245fce-079b-4204-a6a5-ec7c94915004",
                                "sense_id": "d6306228-d9ef-33bd-b4ac-396975e84816",
                                "text": "Current among the Britons, the name of Manchester was equally received and retained by the Saxons. […] [M]oſt of the more remarkable objects about the town, at this period, exchanged their Britiſh denominations for Saxon. And even one of the rivers, even the monarch of the Mancunian currents, now reſigned up its original name of Beliſama, and received another; from the marſhes and marſhy meadows, that ſkirt its channel on both ſides in one continued line to the ſea, obtaining the deſcriptive denomination of Merſc-ey, Merſ-ey, or marſhy water."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35ca8ed6-5332-433f-b978-8ee083bd46f2",
                                "sense_id": "d6306228-d9ef-33bd-b4ac-396975e84816",
                                "text": "The Bridgewater Canal in Manchester during the summer months is colonised every Sunday by hundreds of Mancunian men and boys involved in angling competitions, a very traditional and gendered practice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03e6ae69-c235-4a41-bc18-80906f771211",
                                "sense_id": "d6306228-d9ef-33bd-b4ac-396975e84816",
                                "text": "The Sex Pistols' first performance at Manchester's Lesser Free Trade Hall on June 4, 1976 has become widely accredited as 'year zero' in the history of Mancunian rock music."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3931f734-788f-471e-8e19-da6c5f6ca8bf",
                        "source_entry_id": "6a0dedea-d1c4-3839-a942-8da9042e8c87",
                        "source_sense_id": "d6306228-d9ef-33bd-b4ac-396975e84816",
                        "source_sense_description": "related or pertaining to Manchester, England",
                        "target_lang_word": "mancunien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mancunien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eed1aed2-44df-3c66-bb5c-7a22a47beccb",
                                        "entry_id": "5d1c9d60-6168-34b1-aa59-ea8fa325040c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a un rapport avec Manchester ou ses habitants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0880391f-d517-43d9-b473-ef149662d93d",
                                                "sense_id": "eed1aed2-44df-3c66-bb5c-7a22a47beccb",
                                                "text": "Transféré ensuite à Manchester United, l'un des clubs les plus prestigieux du monde, il s'affirme comme la coqueluche d'Old Trafford, le stade mancunien, baptisé avec une certaine candeur Theater of Dreams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7233920-42c4-405c-8a48-4f5e317c7756",
                                                "sense_id": "eed1aed2-44df-3c66-bb5c-7a22a47beccb",
                                                "text": "Dans deux films de ce siècle retraçant l'épopée de la scène mancunienne de la charnière punk/post-punk (24Hour Party People et Control), on avait été estomaqué par le soin, la maniaquerie avec lesquels était rebâti le Manchester de la fin des années 70/début des années 80."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0ccd99e-89d1-4a4f-a448-e0b62c90d7aa",
                                                "sense_id": "eed1aed2-44df-3c66-bb5c-7a22a47beccb",
                                                "text": "Le derby mancunien entre City et United a largement tourné à l’avantage des Cityzens (6-3)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
